# UI Design System & Component Guidelines

## 1. Tailwind CSS v4 Architecture

- **No `tailwind.config.js`**:
  Tailwind v4 is configured entirely via CSS. Do NOT add `tailwind.config.js` or `tailwind.config.ts`.
- **CSS Custom Property Tokens**:
  All design tokens are defined in `src/styles/theme.css`:
  - Colors: `--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, `--primary-foreground`, `--muted`, `--muted-foreground`, `--border`, `--destructive`, etc.
  - Metrics: `--radius`, `--font-sans`, `--font-mono`.
- **Class Merging**:
  Always use the `cn(...)` utility helper (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) when applying or extending classes:
  ```tsx
  import { cn } from "@/utils";
  
  export function MyComponent({ className, ...props }: ComponentProps) {
    return <div className={cn("base-classes bg-primary text-primary-foreground", className)} {...props} />;
  }
  ```
- **No Inline Styles**:
  Do not use `style={{ ... }}` for static styling, layout, or color assignments. Use Tailwind classes.

## 2. Radix UI & Component Composition

- **Polymorphism with `Slot` (`asChild`)**:
  Interactive primitives (Button, Link, Card triggers) must support the `asChild` prop via Radix UI `@radix-ui/react-slot`:
  ```tsx
  import { Slot } from "@radix-ui/react-slot";
  
  export const Button = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(
    ({ asChild = false, className, ...props }, ref) => {
      const Comp = asChild ? Slot : "button";
      return <Comp ref={ref} className={cn(buttonVariants({ ... }), className)} {...props} />;
    }
  );
  ```
- **Controlled vs Uncontrolled States**:
  Support both controlled (`value`/`onValueChange`) and uncontrolled (`defaultValue`) patterns in input, select, dialog, and tab components.

## 3. Accessibility Standards (WCAG 2.2 AA)

- **Dynamic IDs**: Always use `React.useId()` to generate element IDs:
  ```tsx
  const id = React.useId();
  // <label htmlFor={id}>
  // <input id={id} aria-describedby={`${id}-error`} />
  // <p id={`${id}-error`} role="alert">
  ```
- **Loading & Busy States**:
  Buttons in `isPending` or loading states must show an accessible spinner and announce `aria-busy="true"`.
- **Form Error Association**:
  Invalid inputs must set `aria-invalid="true"` and point `aria-describedby` to the error element.
- **Focus Rings**:
  Never remove outline focus rings without providing an accessible alternative (`focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2`).
- **Touch Targets**:
  Ensure minimum interactive hit targets of >= 24x24px (desktop) and >= 44x44px (mobile touch).
